AnchorsTest
├── anchorZecValue
│   ├── given the anchor's currency has a rate
│   │   └── it prices the anchor in ZEC
│   ├── given the currency has no rate
│   │   └── it cannot price it
│   ├── given the amount is not positive
│   │   └── it cannot price it
│   └── given the arithmetic does not produce a usable number
│       └── it cannot price it
├── compareToAnchors
│   ├── it expresses a price in things the user knows
│   ├── it is invariant to the ZEC price — the whole point
│   ├── it prefers the anchor closest to a countable multiple
│   ├── it works across currencies, because both legs go through ZEC
│   ├── given a comparison nobody can picture
│   │   ├── it drops one that is too small
│   │   └── it drops one that is too large
│   ├── given an anchor in a currency with no rate
│   │   └── it ignores that anchor
│   ├── given the amount is not positive
│   │   └── it returns nothing
│   └── when a limit is given
│       └── it returns no more than that many
├── formatCount
│   ├── given a count in the hundreds
│   │   └── it rounds to a whole number
│   ├── given a count in the tens
│   │   └── it rounds to a whole number
│   ├── given a count around one
│   │   └── it keeps one decimal
│   ├── given a count below one
│   │   └── it keeps two decimals
│   └── when a locale is given
│       └── it formats in that locale
├── formatComparisons
│   ├── it reads as a sentence
│   └── given there is nothing to compare
│       └── it says nothing
├── driftedAnchors
│   ├── it flags an anchor once it moves past the threshold
│   ├── it stays quiet inside the threshold
│   ├── it reports the biggest mover first
│   ├── given the anchor can no longer be priced
│   │   └── it is skipped
│   └── given the anchor was never priced
│       └── it is skipped
└── createAnchor
    ├── it records the ZEC cost at the moment it was set
    ├── it gives each anchor its own id
    ├── it upper-cases the currency
    ├── given a label longer than the field allows
    │   └── it truncates the label
    └── given input it cannot price
        ├── it refuses an empty label
        ├── it refuses a non-positive amount
        └── it refuses a currency with no rate
